{"parentUuid":"029c3480-cd86-4d99-954b-48be92201b79","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MYQqRtiiNgctqgwozdkCgW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Code Review: PR #1114 — Checkpoints v2 migration rerun fixes\n\n## Overview\n\nThree rerun bugs in `entire migrate --checkpoints v2` are addressed:\n\n1. **Duplicate `/full/<n>` archives** on supposed no-ops (one repo grew gen 46 → 86).\n2. **Partial-state recovery** — interrupting between `/main` write and packer flush previously didn't resume cleanly.\n3. **Unconditional transcript walk** on every rerun, even with no work to do.\n\nThree orthogonal performance levers:\n- `BuildFullSessionArtifactsIndex` — one-time tree walk, then O(1) presence lookups (replaces per-session ref-list + tree-walk).\n- `ReadSessionMetadata` — metadata-only read (skips prompts + compact transcript).\n- `RepairV2GenerationMetadata` is now gated on `freshlyPackedRefs > 0`, with newly-packed refs excluded since their `generation.json` is computed in-memory from `AggregateTranscriptTimestamps`.\n\nNet: no-op reruns drop from 20+ minutes to seconds.\n\n## Strengths\n\n- **Good \"why\" comments.** The block comment in `runMigrateCheckpointsV2` explaining the repair-gating tradeoff and the `generationPacker.writtenRefs` doc are exemplary — they describe motivation, cost, and the in-memory shortcut.\n- **Index design is clean.** Build-once / lookup-many is the right shape; `Has()` is nil-safe (covered by `TestV2GitStore_BuildFullSessionArtifactsIndex_NilSafe`); the `_AgreesWithHasFullSessionArtifacts` test pins the contract that the cache and the per-call predicate stay in sync.\n- **Both Copilot review concerns appear addressed** in later commits: (a) `ReadSessionMetadata` now wraps with the fetcher (`v2_read.go:220`, faedaec19), and (b) compact-transcript backfill is preserved on the existing-checkpoint path (`migrate.go:339`, f8a2e3290) — verified by `TestMigrateCheckpointsV2_