rnal one and updating callers, or marking the wrapper with a `// kept for tests` comment so the duplication isn't mysterious.\n\n**6. Comment in `collectMissingFullSessionsForPacking`** says \"(used by tests that don't build an index up front)\" but production always builds it. Make this explicit so future readers don't think there's a real fallback path.\n\n## Test coverage\n\nAdded: resume-on-rerun, no-op-skips-repair, picks-up-new-checkpoints, backfill-when-full-exists, exclude-refs, metadata-fetcher-fallback, index-agrees-with-predicate, index-nil-safe.\n\nRemoved (mostly justified — paths no longer exist): cleanup-v1-transcripts (3), fast-path-fully-migrated, `TestV2CheckpointFullyMigrated`, backfill-skips-v1-when-no-agent, repairs-missing-full-before-backfill.\n\nGap: the partial-repair task-metadata test (see issue 1).\n\n## Risks\n\n- **Touches the migration hot path** for v2 checkpoints — the medium-risk classification from the auto-summary is right.\n- **Large repos with archived refs that need repair-only fixes** are now stuck unless they `--force`, which is destructive for already-good archives. Mitigate with documentation or a dedicated knob.\n- **Concurrent migrations** were not safe before either, but the index makes the staleness window slightly more visible. Worth a one-line \"not safe to run concurrently\" log on start, if not already present.\n\nOverall: solid perf win with a sensible gating decision; the main asks are restoring the partial-repair regression test and offering an escape hatch for repair-only runs."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4600,"cache_read_input_tokens":120782,"output_tokens":2264,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4600,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2264,"cache_read